# Digital Workplace Autopilot — 10-agent network (M7).
# Front man: commander (first entry, LLM only — no class/toolbox).
# Delegation: tools[] down-chains + AAOSA instructions. Commander picks
# specialists per inquiry via route_request ranking — never a fixed chain.
{
    "metadata": {
        "description": "Policy-governed multi-agent digital workplace operations: diagnose, verify, learn, heal."
        "tags": ["operations", "digital-workplace"]
        "sample_queries": [
            "My laptop is extremely slow and Teams keeps freezing.",
            "I changed my password and now my VPN won't connect.",
            "How do I claim internet reimbursement?",
        ]
    },

    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",

    # Single Gemini default (M0 D003). Change model in one place.
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",
    "max_steps": 20000,
    "max_execution_seconds": 1800,
    "error_formatter": "json",
    "error_fragments": ["Error:", "Exception:", "Traceback (most recent call last)"],
    "tools": [
        # 1. FRONT MAN — commander. No parameters by design (user-facing entry).
        {
            "name": "commander",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Front door and orchestrator for digital workplace requests. Receives the
user inquiry, resolves user and device context, ranks specialist agents,
delegates only where useful, and returns one final user-facing response.
"""
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the Digital Workplace Commander. Principle: AI THINKS, TOOLS
OBSERVE, AGENTS COLLABORATE, POLICY AUTHORIZES, TOOLS EXECUTE, AI VERIFIES,
SYSTEM LEARNS, FLEET HEALS.

For each inquiry:
1. Call get_user_context and get_case_context first.
2. Call route_request for a RANKED specialist list, then search_known_workflows.
3. Delegate ONLY to specialists whose rank and reason fit the inquiry. Never
   call every specialist. Technical issues need endpoint/software/network/
   identity plus rca_agent; knowledge questions need knowledge_agent only.
4. If evidence is insufficient, ask rca_agent what is missing and delegate
   follow-up investigation before concluding.
5. Return ONE final response. If confidence is low or evidence conflicts,
   say INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE and escalate instead of guessing.
6. You never execute remediation directly and never authorize actions;
   authorization belongs to the deterministic control plane.
""",
            "tools": ["route_request", "get_user_context", "get_case_context", "search_known_workflows", "endpoint_agent", "software_agent", "network_agent", "identity_agent", "rca_agent", "knowledge_agent", "security_agent", "learning_agent", "servicenow_agent"]
        },
        # 2. Endpoint specialist (Nexthink/Tanium evidence).
        {
            "name": "endpoint_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Laptop health, CPU, RAM, disk, processes, boot, endpoint telemetry.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to investigate"},
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device, e.g. DEVICE_001"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the Endpoint Agent. Use query_device_health first, then let results
guide you: high CPU or RAM means call query_processes; high disk means call
query_disk_health; recent-change suspicion means call query_endpoint_events.
Cross-check Nexthink against Tanium for important claims. Stop when evidence
is sufficient and return normalized findings with device_id and values.
""",
            "tools": ["query_device_health", "query_nexthink", "query_tanium", "query_processes", "query_disk_health", "query_endpoint_events"]
        },
        # 3. Software specialist (Intune evidence).
        {
            "name": "software_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Installed software, versions, updates, app health, install requests, patch history.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to investigate"},
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device, e.g. DEVICE_001"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the Software Agent. Start with query_software_inventory, correlate
unhealthy apps with query_recent_changes and query_patch_history, and use
query_software_catalog only for install requests. Flag version regressions
with before and after versions. Stop when evidence is sufficient.
""",
            "tools": ["query_intune", "query_software_inventory", "query_software_catalog", "query_recent_changes", "query_patch_history"]
        },
        # 4. Network specialist (Zscaler/Cloudflare evidence).
        {
            "name": "network_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "VPN, proxy, DNS, packet loss, connectivity, secure web gateway, routes.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to investigate"},
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device, e.g. DEVICE_001"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the Network Agent. Start with query_network, then follow the fault:
VPN symptoms mean query_vpn_state plus query_zscaler; name resolution means
query_dns; slowness means query_network_path plus query_cloudflare. Isolate
the layer before blaming it. Stop when evidence is sufficient.
""",
            "tools": ["query_network", "query_zscaler", "query_cloudflare", "query_dns", "query_vpn_state", "query_network_path"]
        },
        # 5. Identity specialist (Entra evidence).
        {
            "name": "identity_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Authentication, account state, sign-in events, MFA, lockout, entitlements.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to investigate"},
                        "user_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased user, e.g. USER_001"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the Identity and Access Agent. Start with query_account_state and
query_signin_history, then query_mfa_state for auth failures and
query_access_state for entitlement questions. Distinguish identity faults
from downstream token staleness with timestamps. Stop when sufficient.
""",
            "tools": ["query_entra", "query_signin_history", "query_account_state", "query_mfa_state", "query_access_state"]
        },
        # 6. RCA fusion (competing hypotheses, calibrated confidence).
        {
            "name": "rca_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Correlate multi-system evidence into competing hypotheses with confidence.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to diagnose"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the RCA and Diagnostic Fusion Agent. Never merely summarize. Build
competing hypotheses with generate_hypotheses, test each with
score_hypothesis and check_confidence_threshold, correlate with
correlate_evidence, consult search_runbooks and search_past_incidents, and
render the causal chain with build_causal_graph.

Output shape:
HYPOTHESIS 1, Evidence, Confidence, SUPPORTED or REJECTED, repeated per
hypothesis, then the final call. Reject red herrings explicitly with the
evidence that refutes them. At 90 or above you may proceed under policy;
70 to 89 needs human confirmation; below 70, or on conflicting or missing
mandatory evidence, conclude INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE and escalate. Never
invent nodes without tool evidence.
""",
            "tools": ["correlate_evidence", "generate_hypotheses", "score_hypothesis", "search_runbooks", "search_past_incidents", "check_confidence_threshold", "build_causal_graph"]
        },
        # 7. Knowledge specialist (permission-aware).
        {
            "name": "knowledge_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "HR, Finance, IT, Security and application policy, process and runbook knowledge.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to look up"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the Knowledge Agent. Retrieval is permission-aware: pass the caller
role on every call, check get_document_access_context before quoting, and
never let unauthorized content enter the conversation. Answer with the
answer, source document, relevant section, and confidence via
cite_knowledge_source. Denied documents get ACCESS DENIED, never excerpts.
""",
            "tools": ["search_enterprise_knowledge", "get_document_access_context", "cite_knowledge_source"]
        },
        # 8. Security advisor (advises; never authorizes).
        {
            "name": "security_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Security rules, device compliance, sensitive-action and control requirements.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to assess"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the Security and Compliance Advisor. Interpret posture with
get_security_context and check_device_compliance, and requirements with
check_compliance_requirements and check_privileged_action_requirements.
You ADVISE only. Final execution authorization belongs to the deterministic
coded control plane and you must never grant it yourself.
""",
            "tools": ["get_security_context", "check_device_compliance", "check_compliance_requirements", "check_privileged_action_requirements"]
        },
        # 9. Learning specialist (proposes; never self-approves).
        {
            "name": "learning_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Repeated-resolution patterns and governed reusable workflow candidates.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to learn from"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the Learning and Workflow Agent. Record outcomes with
record_resolution_pattern, detect repeats with detect_workflow_pattern and
get_workflow_statistics, propose reuse with create_workflow_candidate, and
recall registry state with search_workflow_registry. You NEVER approve your
own candidate; every candidate needs human approval before use.
""",
            "tools": ["record_resolution_pattern", "detect_workflow_pattern", "create_workflow_candidate", "search_workflow_registry", "get_workflow_statistics"]
        },
        # 10. ServiceNow coordinator (incident/problem lifecycle).
        {
            "name": "servicenow_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "ServiceNow incident and problem lifecycle via the Table API.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "What to record"}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${aaosa_instructions} """
You are the ServiceNow Coordinator. Own the incident lifecycle with
create_incident, get_incident, search_incidents, add_work_note,
update_incident, resolve_incident and escalate_incident, plus fleet-wide
patterns with create_problem and link_incident_to_problem. Resolve only
when verification evidence is present in the inquiry, never on execution
alone. Credentials stay server-side; you only pass business fields.
""",
            "tools": ["create_incident", "get_incident", "search_incidents", "add_work_note", "update_incident", "resolve_incident", "escalate_incident", "create_problem", "link_incident_to_problem"]
        },
        # ---- coded tools: commander ----
        {
            "name": "route_request",
            "class": "digital_workplace.commander_tools.RouteRequest",
            "function": {
                "description": "Rank specialist agents for an inquiry with reasons. Ranked, never a fixed chain.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request_text": {"type": "string", "description": "User inquiry"}
                    },
                    "required": ["request_text"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "get_user_context",
            "class": "digital_workplace.commander_tools.GetUserContext",
            "function": {
                "description": "Resolve user, device, role and department for an aliased user.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "user_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased user, e.g. USER_001"},
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device override"}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "get_case_context",
            "class": "digital_workplace.commander_tools.GetCaseContext",
            "function": {
                "description": "Load a case row by case_id from local state.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "case_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Case id"}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "search_known_workflows",
            "class": "digital_workplace.commander_tools.SearchKnownWorkflows",
            "function": {
                "description": "Find approved reusable workflows by failure signature. Candidates excluded.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "failure_signature": {"type": "string", "description": "Failure signature"}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            }
        },
        # ---- coded tools: endpoint ----
        {
            "name": "query_device_health",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryDeviceHealth",
            "function": {
                "description": "Device CPU, RAM, disk, boot and compliance from Nexthink.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_nexthink",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryNexthink",
            "function": {
                "description": "Nexthink experience view for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_tanium",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryTanium",
            "function": {
                "description": "Tanium live view for a device (cross-checks Nexthink).",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_processes",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryProcesses",
            "function": {
                "description": "Top processes with memory and CPU for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_disk_health",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryDiskHealth",
            "function": {
                "description": "Disk utilization and health status for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_endpoint_events",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryEndpointEvents",
            "function": {
                "description": "Recent endpoint changes and events for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        # ---- coded tools: software ----
        {
            "name": "query_intune",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryIntune",
            "function": {
                "description": "Intune software summary with unhealthy apps for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_software_inventory",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QuerySoftwareInventory",
            "function": {
                "description": "Full installed-software inventory for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_software_catalog",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QuerySoftwareCatalog",
            "function": {
                "description": "Requestable software catalog, optionally filtered by name.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "query": {"type": "string", "description": "Name filter"}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_recent_changes",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryRecentChanges",
            "function": {
                "description": "Recent software changes for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_patch_history",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryPatchHistory",
            "function": {
                "description": "OS and app patch history for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        # ---- coded tools: network ----
        {
            "name": "query_network",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryNetwork",
            "function": {
                "description": "Network health: latency, loss, DNS, proxy and path.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_zscaler",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryZscaler",
            "function": {
                "description": "Zscaler secure-access view with VPN state.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_cloudflare",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryCloudflare",
            "function": {
                "description": "Cloudflare path and DNS view for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_dns",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryDns",
            "function": {
                "description": "DNS resolution health for a device.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_vpn_state",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryVpnState",
            "function": {
                "description": "VPN connection state, gateway and last error.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_network_path",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryNetworkPath",
            "function": {
                "description": "Network path quality: route, latency and loss.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "device_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased device"}
                    },
                    "required": ["device_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        # ---- coded tools: identity ----
        {
            "name": "query_entra",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryEntra",
            "function": {
                "description": "Entra identity state for an aliased user.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "user_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased user"}
                    },
                    "required": ["user_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_signin_history",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QuerySigninHistory",
            "function": {
                "description": "Recent sign-in events for an aliased user.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "user_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased user"},
                        "limit": {"type": "integer", "description": "Max events"}
                    },
                    "required": ["user_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_account_state",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryAccountState",
            "function": {
                "description": "Account state and lockout for an aliased user.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "user_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased user"}
                    },
                    "required": ["user_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_mfa_state",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryMfaState",
            "function": {
                "description": "MFA enrollment and health for an aliased user.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "user_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased user"}
                    },
                    "required": ["user_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "query_access_state",
            "class": "digital_workplace.observe.QueryAccessState",
            "function": {
                "description": "Access decision inputs for an aliased user.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "user_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Aliased user"}
                    },
                    "required": ["user_id"]
                }
            }
        },
        # ---- coded tools: rca ----
        {
            "name": "correlate_evidence",
            "class": "digital_workplace.rca.CorrelateEvidence",
            "function": {
                "description": "Group evidence by entity and flag change-adjacent items.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "evidence": {"type": "array", "description": "Evidence objects with evidence_id"}
                    },
                    "required": ["evidence"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "generate_hypotheses",
            "class": "digital_workplace.rca.GenerateHypotheses",
            "function": {
                "description": "Draft candidate hypotheses from evidence signals for judging.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "evidence": {"type": "array", "description": "Evidence objects"}
                    },
                    "required": ["evidence"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "score_hypothesis",
            "class": "digital_workplace.rca.ScoreHypothesis",
            "function": {
                "description": "Score one hypothesis from supporting and refuting evidence counts.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "supporting": {"type": "array", "description": "Supporting evidence ids"},
                        "refuting": {"type": "array", "description": "Refuting evidence ids"}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "search_runbooks",
            "class": "digital_workplace.rca.SearchRunbooks",
            "function": {
                "description": "Search approved runbooks by query text.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "query": {"type": "string", "description": "Query text"}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "search_past_incidents",
            "class": "digital_workplace.rca.SearchPastIncidents",
            "function": {
                "description": "Find past local incidents matching a signature.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "signature": {"type": "string", "description": "Signature text"}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "check_confidence_threshold",
            "class": "digital_workplace.rca.CheckConfidenceThreshold",
            "function": {
                "description": "Map confidence to proceed, confirm or escalate.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "confidence": {"type": "number", "description": "Confidence 0-100"}
                    },
                    "required": ["confidence"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "build_causal_graph",
            "class": "digital_workplace.rca.BuildCausalGraph",
            "function": {
                "description": "Build an evidence-backed causal graph with Mermaid output.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "evidence": {"type": "array", "description": "Evidence objects"},
                        "root_cause": {"type": "string", "description": "Root cause label"}
                    },
                    "required": ["evidence"]
                }
            }
        },
        # ---- coded tools: knowledge ----
        {
            "name": "search_enterprise_knowledge",
            "class": "digital_workplace.knowledge.SearchEnterpriseKnowledge",
            "function": {
                "description": "Search authorized knowledge for a role. Unauthorized docs never surface.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "query": {"type": "string", "description": "Query text"},
                        "user_role": {"type": "string", "description": "Caller role"}
                    },
                    "required": ["query"]
                }
            }
